# ADR-0008: Field Schemas for the Provenance Layer and Term/Motif Ledger

## Status

**Open.** This ADR proposes two independent, separately-decidable field-level schema additions, not one accept/reject decision. See "Recommendation" for the per-item call and "Next action" for what closes it.

> **Numbering note:** `docs/adr/` currently has two files both numbered 0007 (`0007-reader-accessibility-register-and-clarity-pass-from-bac-thread.md` and `0007-transformation-fidelity-and-readability-assist-concepts.md`). This ADR takes the next unused number, 0008, without renumbering either 0007 file. The owner should resolve that collision separately — it is out of scope for this ADR.

## Context

On 2026-08-19 the project owner pasted a ChatGPT thread (source: the "Magnus Progenitor Saga" custom GPT project) into a Cowork session, scavenged per the same scope rule already applied twice to this property's source material (see ADR-0005 and ADR-0006): extract architecture signal only, exclude the property's own narrative, branding, and business content. That extraction is archived at `docs/thread-extracts/mps-bac-content-ops-schema-signals.md`.

Two items already logged as open in this repository — ADR-0005 item 2 (a side-car provenance layer on capsules/scenes) and ADR-0006 item 2 (a steward-facing term/motif ledger) — are currently proposals with no field list. Both are blocked on the same missing prerequisite: the `capsules` table, which does not exist yet per ADR-0004's finding. The new source material supplies concrete database schemas for both from a working system (not a design exercise), which this ADR restates as TF-specific field proposals.

## Reaffirmed, not reopened

The source material's own recommended architecture is Notion-centric (nine Notion databases feeding GitHub as a secondary archive). This is the third piece of MPS/BAC-sourced material to independently propose that shape (see ADR-0005's "Reaffirmed, not reopened" and the corresponding note in `[[telling_forward_gemini_thread_context]]`). TF's 2026-08-17 confirmed decision — GitHub-only, capsules as GitHub Issues, no Notion dependency — stands. This ADR proposes field *shapes*, to live in TF's own `capsules` table (or equivalent), not the Notion database structure they were observed in.

## Concepts extended into concrete proposals

### 1. Provenance field schema (concretizes ADR-0005 item 2)

ADR-0005 item 2 proposes "a lightweight, optional provenance record on every capsule/scene... which tier or engine produced or matured it," without a field list. The source material's "Revision Runs / Maturity" and "AI Council Outputs" schemas supply one.

**Proposal — provenance fields to reserve on the `capsules` table (or a linked provenance record), when that table is designed:**

| Field | Type / values | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `produced_by_tier` | enum: `tier_0_rules`, `tier_1_actions_phi4`, `tier_2_byo_ai`, `human` | Which ingestion tier (ADR-0004) or manual entry produced this capsule |
| `matured_by_engine` | enum: `PME`, `PIE`, `CME`, `CIE`, `none` | Which engine, if any, matured or inverted this capsule |
| `maturity_rung_before` / `maturity_rung_after` | `R0`–`R10` | PME rung progression, if matured — already-confirmed TF lineage concept, not previously stored as structured data anywhere in this repo |
| `human_edited_after` | boolean | Whether a human modified the output after generation, per Mission principle #9 ("agents... do not silently claim authorship") |
| `accepted` | boolean / null | Whether the steward accepted this version into canon |
| `source_reference` | text (GitHub commit SHA, PR number, or Issue reference) | Traceable link back to the concrete change, consistent with this repo's "Postgres is a derived cache over GitHub-native objects" pattern (per `telling_forward_ingestion_and_mcp.md`) |

This is a direct extension of ADR-0005's existing recommendation ("reserve the field now, defer the UI") — the fields above are what "the field" concretely means.

### 2. Term/motif ledger field schema (concretizes ADR-0006 item 2)

ADR-0006 item 2 proposes "a lightweight, derived... per-entity record — origin, current canon status, change log," without a field list. The source material's "Canon Terms / Glossary" schema supplies one, trimmed to what ADR-0006 already scoped as read-only steward tooling (not the source system's single-author saturation/cadence-scoring machinery, which ADR-0006 already excluded as a non-fit).

**Proposal — fields for the derived, per-entity term/motif ledger:**

| Field | Type / values | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `term_or_entity` | text | The named character, place, or invented term |
| `canon_status` | enum: `proposed`, `active`, `locked`, `deprecated` | Same status vocabulary already implied by ADR-0006's "stable enough to be treated as locked" |
| `first_appearance` | reference (capsule/scene ID) | Origin point, derived from capsule metadata — not separately authored |
| `drift_risk` | enum: `low`, `medium`, `high` | Steward-facing signal for terms extended inconsistently across independent contributors — the exact multi-contributor problem ADR-0006 names |
| `related_entities` / `related_motifs` | references | Cross-links, derived from capsule tagging |

This ledger stays **read-only and derived**, per ADR-0006's existing scope — no new authoring surface, no fields beyond what's needed to make drift visible to a steward.

## Non-goals of this ADR

- Does not authorize building the `capsules` table itself — that remains a prerequisite owned by whatever ADR or spec eventually designs it (flagged in ADR-0004, ADR-0005, and ADR-0006 as a shared blocker).
- Does not adopt the source system's Notion database structure, its saturation/cadence scoring, or its execution-hierarchy machinery — consistent with ADR-0006's existing exclusion of that material as a single-author-system fit problem.
- Does not resolve the ADR numbering collision at 0007/0007 — noted above, left to the owner.
- Does not propose a frontmatter YAML standard for scene/capsule markdown files — that idea is logged in `docs/thread-extracts/mps-bac-content-ops-schema-signals.md`'s Open Questions as a separate, undecided question (engineering spec vs. ADR track), not folded into this ADR.

## Recommendation

| Item | Recommendation |
|---|---|
| 1. Provenance field schema | Accept design intent; adopt this field list as the starting point when the `capsules` table is designed, subject to owner review |
| 2. Term/motif ledger field schema | Accept design intent; adopt this field list as the starting point for ADR-0006 item 2's ledger, subject to owner review |

## Consequences

- When the `capsules` table is finally designed, its first schema version should account for both field lists above rather than retrofitting them later — the same "reserve now, build later" pattern already used in ADR-0005 and ADR-0006.
- Neither item authorizes any code, schema, or UI work on its own. Both remain blocked on the `capsules` table's actual design.

## Next action

The project owner should give a per-item call — accept, adapt, or reject — for the two field lists above, and separately decide whether to resolve the 0007/0007 ADR numbering collision. Update this ADR's Status once that call is made.
